WEBVTT

NOTE F3: two people (Dev, Aisha) share one connection labelled "Meeting Room 2" and agree throughout. Synthetic.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
<v Interviewer>Thanks both. Could you describe how you set up a laptop for a new starter?</v>

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Dev here. So the goal is the new person can log in and work on day one, no faffing about.</v>

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Aisha here. Yeah, that's exactly it. Day one, ready to go.</v>

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Meeting Room 2>It starts when HR raises a new starter ticket, usually a week before they join.</v>

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:42.000
<v Meeting Room 2>We pick a laptop from the stock cupboard and record the serial number against their name in the asset system.</v>

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Same for me, I do exactly that. The asset system then links it to their account.</v>

7
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:59.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Then we image it with the standard build. That takes about an hour, mostly waiting.</v>

8
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Agreed, an hour. You just leave it running.</v>

9
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Interviewer>Do you ever do it differently from each other?</v>

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Not really, we wrote the checklist together.</v>

11
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
<v Meeting Room 2>No, we both follow the checklist.</v>

12
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:27.000
<v Meeting Room 2>On their first morning we hand it over and they sign the asset form.</v>

13
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Once they've logged in successfully we close the ticket.</v>

14
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.000
<v Interviewer>How often does this come up?</v>

15
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:45.000
<v Meeting Room 2>Pretty much every week. Sometimes three or four in a week.</v>
